{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>When the Most High gave nations their inheritance, when He separated the children of man.</b> From here on he begins to recount the deeds of kindness that the Holy One, blessed be He, performed for Israel in exalting them above all the peoples, and He showed that Israel are weighed against all of them. Regarding this he said: ״בְּהַנְחֵל עֶלְיוֹן גּוֹיִם״ — when He apportioned the world as an inheritance to all the nations, at that very time He separated and set apart Abraham from them and said to him: ״לֶךְ לְךָ מֵאַרְצְךָ״ (Genesis 12:1). This is what he said: ״בְּהַפְרִידוֹ בְּנֵי אָדָם״ — for you are called אָדָם and not the nations. And the Holy One, blessed be He, separated them from the nations and took them to one side. And ״יַצֵּב גְּבוּלוֹת עַמִּים לְמִסְפַּר בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — seventy nations corresponding to the seventy souls of Jacob, for by this He showed that each individual among them is weighed against an entire nation, as explained in the Akeidah, parashat בְּהַעֲלֹתְךָ, on the verse (Psalms 87:4–5): ״אַזְכִּיר רַהַב וּבָבֶל וְגוֹ׳, וּלְצִיּוֹן יֵאָמַר אִישׁ וְאִישׁ יֻלַּד בָּהּ״." "<b>For the portion of HaShem is His people, etc.</b> He showed that through three kinds of number the Holy One, blessed be He, demonstrated Israel's belovedness, for they are weighed against all of existence. The first number: our fathers went down to Egypt with seventy souls, corresponding to seventy nations and seventy heavenly princes. Regarding this He said: ״יַצֵּב גְּבֻלֹת עַמִּים לְמִסְפַּר בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״. The second number: that is the twelve tribes of Israel, corresponding to the twelve constellations which HaShem apportioned to all the peoples, as written in parashat וָאֶתְחַנַּן (4:19): ״וּפֶן תִּשָּׂא עֵינֶיךָ הַשָּׁמַיְמָה וְרָאִיתָ אֶת הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ וְגוֹ׳ אֲשֶׁר חָלַק ה׳ לְכָל הָעַמִּים״. Corresponding to this He said here: ״כִּי חֵלֶק ה׳ עַמּוֹ״ — meaning that those twelve constellations He delivered as the portion of all the peoples; yet ״חֵלֶק ה׳ עַמּוֹ״, for they too, in the number of the twelve tribes of Israel, shall be portion for portion equal to equal. The third number: that is three worlds, which encompass all of existence. Regarding this He said: ״יַעֲקֹב חֶבֶל נַחֲלָתוֹ״ — just as this חֶבֶל is tripled, so He established three patriarchs as the foundation for all of existence."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:15:48.451601518Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}